# DESCRIPTION

k1-syscon drives two of the SpacemiT K1's system controllers, the units that gate its devices' clocks and hold them in reset: the APBC, at `0xd4015000`, for the peripherals on the APB (the UARTs, I2C, PWM, GPIO, SPI), and the APMU, at `0xd4282800`, for the application subsystem's (the EMACs, SDHCIs, USB, PCIe, DMA, display).
devmgr(8) starts it for each, before the devices that link to it, by its record:

```text
driver k1-syscon
class clock
match dt spacemit,k1-syscon-apbc
match dt spacemit,k1-syscon-apmu
```

It reads its node's `compatible` at `/dev/dt/compatible` to know which unit it has, and uses the first of its registers.
A device's `clocks` and `resets` name the unit and an id, the ids of `dt-bindings/clock/spacemit,k1-syscon.h`: the K1's first Ethernet MAC has the APMU's clock 37 (`emac0_bus`) and reset 35.
devmgr gives the unit's tree to that device's driver at `/dev/provider/<service>`, and its `/dev/dt/links` says which ids are the device's (devmgr(8)).

A clock is a gate, a mask of bits in its unit's control register: `on` sets them all, `off` clears them.
A clock with no gate (a fixed factor, a mux or a divider alone, such as the APMU's `pmua_aclk`) is always on.
The APMU's three SDHCI clocks, 11 to 13 (`sdh0`, `sdh1`, `sdh2`), also take a rate: each is one of its parents divided by 1 to 8, and `rate` picks the first parent and divider that make exactly the rate asked, sets them with the unit's frequency-change bit, and waits up to 5 ms for the hardware to clear it.
Their parents are PLL1 (2457.6 MHz) divided by 6, 4, 11, 13 or 23 (and 3 for `sdh2`), and two from PLL2, which `rate` doesn't use: 204.8 MHz is PLL1's 409.6 MHz halved.
A reset is asserted by writing its assert bits under its mask and released by writing its release bits: most of the APBC's are a reset bit, set while asserted, and most of the APMU's a release bit, clear while asserted.
Each change reads the register and writes it back with only those bits changed, one command at a time.
The APMU also holds each Ethernet MAC's control register, at `0x3e4` for the first and `0x3ec` for the second, which the MAC's node names by its `spacemit,apmu` offset, and after it the MAC's delay lines: `emac` sets the MAC's interface, RGMII or RMII, its reference and transmit clocks taken from the PHY, and for RGMII each delay line on with a code in steps of 15.6 ps (k1-emac(3) gives its node's `tx-internal-delay-ps` and `rx-internal-delay-ps`).
The first MAC's bus clock and reset are bits of that register too, so they are written only here.
It holds each PCIe controller's control register too, at `0x3cc`, `0x3d4` and `0x3dc`, which the controller's node names by its `spacemit,apmu` offset, and its control logic's after it: `pcie` sets or clears one of the bits k1-pcie(3) drives, the LTSSM's enable (`ltssm`), auxiliary power present (`aux-power`), PERST# asserted (`perst`), the PHY held in reset (`hold-phy`), root complex mode (`rc`) and the controller's soft reset (`soft-reset`); and `combo` gives the combo PHY to PCIe 0 or to USB 3 (k1-pcie-phy(3)).
The APBC has 102 clocks and 51 resets, the APMU 62 clocks and 53 resets.

# FILES

The tree is served in devmgr(8)'s, at `drivers/k1-syscon-dt-system-controller@d4282800` for the APMU, and at `/dev/provider/<service>` in the drivers of the devices that link to it.

: `ctl`
  Takes a command a line: `clock <id> on|off`, `clock <id> rate <hz>`, `reset <id> assert|deassert`, `emac <offset> rgmii|rmii <tx> <rx>`, a MAC's control register and its delay codes (0 to 255), `pcie <offset> ltssm|aux-power|perst|hold-phy|rc|soft-reset on|off`, or `combo pcie|usb`, numbers in decimal or `0x` hexadecimal.
  A line it can't parse, an id or a MAC's or PCIe controller's offset the unit doesn't have, `off` for a clock with no gate, or a rate no parent and divider make exactly fails the write as invalid, as does a rate change the hardware doesn't finish, and the driver logs which.
: `status`
  Read only.
  The unit, `apmu: 62 clocks, 53 resets`; then a line for each clock and each reset as its register reads now, `clock 37 emac0_bus on` (`off`, or `ungated` for one with no gate) and `reset 35 emac0 deasserted` (or `asserted`); then a line for each SDHCI clock's rate as its mux and divider read now, `rate 11 sdh0 204800000` (or `unknown`, from PLL2); then a line for each MAC, `emac 0x3e4 rgmii tx 0 rx 0`; then a line for each PCIe controller, the bits `pcie` sets that are set, `pcie 0x3d4 perst hold-phy rc` (`-` for none), and the combo PHY's, `combo pcie` or `combo usb`; then `commands <n>, failed <n>`, and `last failure: <command>: <why>`, the why `no such id`, `no gate`, `no parent and divider make that rate` or `the change didn't take`.

